{"body":{"from":[{"$ref":"01M6RBNT5FN0JH2X64E5CC7HJR"}],"opens":"A branch is a store, and unlike git's, relational: no longer stale, still a branch, seen from the front as a whole rather than from the side as a fork; this series itself a store of its own. A valuable future development of the store.","restsOn":["taking a whole away as a store","how stores relate to the stores they branched from"],"stands":"noted","title":"A branch as a store"},"id":"01M6RBNTRD3HHH64VCH3MZ8GMA","instance":["01M6RBNRG7D2ZC5P6JEVK0SY5G"],"kind":"version","prev":null}
{"body":{"from":[{"$ref":"01M6RBNT5FN0JH2X64E5CC7HJR"},{"$ref":"01M6RBNT6P5Y6W2XMCC1BDJNDQ"},{"$ref":"01M6RBNTAVMCBF0HJDEJFTTWSX"}],"opens":"Not login but proof: a commit's hash set into a public chain proves a series of events was observed in a particular way from a certain point in time, and no one can mask over it after; only the hash goes public, the store stays its owner's.","restsOn":["signing commits by key","which public chain, and what anchoring costs"],"stands":"noted","title":"History anchored in public"},"id":"01M6RBNTRESVBEG4B1W8GFKWNG","instance":["01M6RBNRG7D2ZC5P6JEVK0SY5G"],"kind":"version","prev":null}
